### =============================================
### RETURN WORKFLOWS COMPREHENSIVE DEMO
### =============================================
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates workflow chaining and advanced state management
### AUDIENCE: Perfect for showcasing return processing and external event handling
### SCENARIOS: Covers standard, defective, expedited, and high-value returns
### MONITORING: Real-time notifications for return workflow tracking
### DURATION: Allow 8-12 minutes for full demonstration
### =============================================

### =============================================
### PHASE 1: SYSTEM PREPARATION
### =============================================

### 1. Health check for returns service
### Expected: Service should be running and healthy
GET http://localhost:3008/health

### 2. Check inventory levels (for restocking validation)
### Expected: Current inventory state for return processing
GET http://localhost:3013/api/v1/inventory

### =============================================
### PHASE 2: STANDARD RETURN PROCESSING
### =============================================

### 3. Submit a standard return request (sequential processing)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates basic return workflow with validation and processing
### MONITORING: Watch notifications UI (localhost:8080) for [RETURN] prefixed messages
### EXPECTED: Return → Validation → Refund → Restock sequence
// @name standard_return
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_john_abc123",
  "customer": "john",
  "item": "apple",
  "reason": "wrong_size",
  "description": "Item was too small",
  "return_value": 75.0
}

### 4. Get standard return status
### PURPOSE: Monitor return workflow progression through states
### EXPECTED: Shows validation → processing → completion stages
@standard_return_id = {{standard_return.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{standard_return_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 3: DEFECTIVE ITEM RETURN (NO RESTOCKING)
### =============================================

### 5. Submit a defective item return
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates defective return child workflow (disposal path)
### MONITORING: Watch for defective-specific processing notifications
### EXPECTED: Full refund without inventory restocking (item disposed)
// @name defective_return
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_sarah_xyz789",
  "customer": "sarah",
  "item": "orange",
  "reason": "defective",
  "description": "Item arrived damaged",
  "return_value": 45.0
}

### 6. Get defective return status
### PURPOSE: Verify defective return processing path
### EXPECTED: Refund processed but no inventory restocking
@defective_return_id = {{defective_return.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{defective_return_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 4: HIGH-VALUE RETURN (APPROVAL WORKFLOW)
### =============================================

### 7. Submit a high-value return (requires manager approval)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates external event handling with timeout
### MONITORING: Watch for approval requirement notifications
### EXPECTED: Return waits for external approval event (24-hour timeout)
// @name high_value_return
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_alice_def456",
  "customer": "alice",
  "item": "kiwi",
  "reason": "not_as_described",
  "description": "Product quality not as expected",
  "return_value": 850.0
}

### 8. Get high-value return status (check for approval requirement)
### PURPOSE: Verify return is waiting for manager approval
### EXPECTED: Status shows pending approval with timeout information
@high_value_return_id = {{high_value_return.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{high_value_return_id}}

### 9. Approve the high-value return
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate external event handling for workflow continuation
### EXPECTED: Return proceeds with processing after approval
@high_value_return_id = {{high_value_return.response.body.instance_id}}

POST http://localhost:3008/returns/{{high_value_return_id}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approver": "manager_jane",
  "approved": true
}

### 10. Check approved return status
### PURPOSE: Verify return processing continues after approval
### EXPECTED: Return moves from pending to processing/completed
@high_value_return_id = {{high_value_return.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{high_value_return_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 5: EXPEDITED RETURN (PARALLEL PROCESSING)
### =============================================

### 11. Submit an expedited return (changed mind - parallel processing)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates parallel refund and restocking for fast completion
### MONITORING: Watch for parallel processing notifications
### EXPECTED: Refund and inventory restocking happen simultaneously
// @name expedited_return
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_bob_ghi789",
  "customer": "bob",
  "item": "pear",
  "reason": "changed_mind",
  "description": "No longer needed",
  "return_value": 120.0
}

### 12. Get expedited return status
### PURPOSE: Monitor parallel processing completion
### EXPECTED: Faster completion due to parallel execution
@expedited_return_id = {{expedited_return.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{expedited_return_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 6: RETURN APPROVAL REJECTION SCENARIO
### =============================================

### 13. Submit another high-value return for rejection testing
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate approval rejection workflow
### MONITORING: Watch for rejection handling notifications
// @name rejection_test_return
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_chaos_demo_user_2_ns43g",
  "customer": "chaos_demo_user_2",
  "item": "kiwi",
  "reason": "not_satisfied",
  "description": "Product did not meet expectations",
  "return_value": 950.0
}

### 14. Reject the high-value return
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate external event rejection handling
### EXPECTED: Return workflow handles rejection and notifies customer
@rejection_test_return_id = {{rejection_test_return.response.body.instance_id}}

POST http://localhost:3008/returns/{{rejection_test_return_id}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approver": "manager_jane",
  "approved": false
}

### 15. Check rejected return status
### PURPOSE: Verify rejection handling and workflow completion
### EXPECTED: Return shows rejected status with manager information
@rejection_test_return_id = {{rejection_test_return.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{rejection_test_return_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 7: COMPREHENSIVE RETURN SCENARIO TESTING
### =============================================

### 16. Submit multiple return types simultaneously (stress test)
### PURPOSE: Test concurrent return processing capabilities
### MONITORING: Observe parallel return workflow handling

// @name concurrent_standard
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_test_user_1",
  "customer": "test_user_1",
  "item": "apple",
  "reason": "wrong_item",
  "description": "Received wrong product",
  "return_value": 55.0
}

### 17. Another concurrent return
// @name concurrent_defective
POST http://localhost:3008/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_order_id": "order_test_user_2",
  "customer": "test_user_2",
  "item": "orange",
  "reason": "defective",
  "description": "Product was damaged",
  "return_value": 40.0
}

### 18. Monitor concurrent processing
@concurrent_standard_id = {{concurrent_standard.response.body.instance_id}}
@concurrent_defective_id = {{concurrent_defective.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{concurrent_standard_id}}

### 19. Monitor second concurrent return
GET http://localhost:3008/returns/{{concurrent_defective_id}}

### =============================================
### RETURN WORKFLOW DEMONSTRATION POINTS
### =============================================
###
### 🎯 KEY FEATURES TO HIGHLIGHT:
###
### 1. WORKFLOW CHAINING & STATE MANAGEMENT:
###    - Returns reference and validate against original orders
###    - Complex state transitions: validation → approval → processing → completion
###    - Persistent state management throughout multi-step process
###    - External event integration with timeouts and fallbacks
###
### 2. ADVANCED ACTIVITY NAMING:
###    - announce_return_request_received: Clear workflow entry point
###    - announce_return_validation_started: Eligibility checking phase
###    - announce_return_approval_required: High-value return detection
###    - announce_return_child_workflow_spawned: Type-specific processing
###    - announce_defective_return_started: Defective item workflow
###    - announce_standard_refund_processing: Standard return path
###    - announce_expedited_parallel_processing: Fast-track processing
###
### 3. DYNAMIC CHILD WORKFLOWS BY RETURN TYPE:
###    - DEFECTIVE: Full refund, no restocking (disposal path)
###    - STANDARD: Sequential refund then inventory restocking
###    - EXPEDITED: Parallel refund and restocking for speed
###    - HIGH-VALUE: External approval event handling
###
### 4. EXTERNAL EVENT HANDLING:
###    - Manager approval system for returns >$500
###    - 24-hour approval timeout with automatic rejection
###    - Approval/rejection event processing
###    - Workflow continuation after external events
###
### 5. PARALLEL PROCESSING OPTIMIZATION:
###    - Expedited returns use parallel execution
###    - Concurrent refund and inventory operations
###    - Performance optimization for time-sensitive returns
###    - Resource efficient parallel activity coordination
###
### 6. COMPREHENSIVE VALIDATION:
###    - Time-based return eligibility (30-day window)
###    - Value threshold validation for approvals
###    - Business rule enforcement and validation
###    - Original order reference validation
###
### 7. REAL-TIME MONITORING:
###    - Live notifications with [RETURN] prefix
###    - State transition tracking and progress updates
###    - Approval workflow status monitoring
###    - Child workflow coordination visibility
###
### 8. FAILURE HANDLING & COMPENSATION:
###    - Timeout handling for approval workflows
###    - Compensation patterns for failed operations
###    - Graceful degradation for service failures
###    - Audit trail for approval/rejection decisions
###
### =============================================
### 🚀 DEMO EXECUTION GUIDE:
###
### TIMING: Execute requests with 15-20 second delays for observation
### MONITORING: Keep notifications UI (localhost:8080) open during demo
### OBSERVATION: Watch for return type-specific processing paths
### ANALYSIS: Use return IDs to trace complete workflow lifecycle
### APPROVAL: Use actual return IDs from responses for approval/rejection
###
### EXPECTED DEMO DURATION: 8-12 minutes for complete demonstration
### CONCURRENT RETURNS: Multiple return types can process simultaneously
### NOTIFICATION RATE: Expect 8-15 events per return workflow
### APPROVAL TIMEOUT: 24 hours for high-value returns (demo: use manual approval)
### =============================================
